  Source: check
  Severity: DiagnosticSeverity_Error
  Code: <none>
  Message:
    `monthly_rent` is a field of `Tenant` only.
    But the value it is read from could also be `Landlord`, which has no `monthly_rent`.

    Nothing narrows it: the value is a projection, not a name, so there is no
    binder for a branch to narrow, and every constructor of `Actor`
    can reach this read.

    Give it a name, then narrow the name:

      CONSIDER v WHEN Tenant t THEN … v's monthly_rent …
      WHERE v MEANS <that value>

    or match the payload directly, which needs no name at all:

      CONSIDER <that value> WHEN Tenant t THEN t

    or declare `monthly_rent` on `Landlord` too.

